<title>BRAZIL: Brazil to issue 500 bln lire Eurobond in May.</title>
<headline>Brazil to issue 500 bln lire Eurobond in May.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil will issue a 500 billion lire 10-year Eurobond in May, to be lead managed by Deutsche Bank, said Marcio Cartier, a consultant to the Brazilian Central Bank's director of international affairs.  </p>
<p>Cartier told reporters the bond was equivalent to about $300 million.</p>
<p>The bond will be Brazil's second sovereign issue this year following a well-received 1.0 billion mark Eurobond in early February.</p>
<p>((-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358))</p>
